# Addresses, numbers and postcodes PERMITTED in this public repo.
#
# scripts/check-public-repo-secrets.py detects personal data by SHAPE and
# suppresses it by this list, so the default for anything not listed is BLOCK.
# Only a human-reviewed entry can separate a published or synthetic value from
# someone's personal data.
#
# Entry forms:
#   @domain.tld          every address at that domain
#   name@domain.tld      one exact address
#   +44 7700 900123      one exact phone number (separators ignored on compare)
#   SW1A 1AA             one exact postcode
#
# RFC 2606 / 6761 reserved names (example.com/.net/.org, .example, .invalid,
# .test, .localhost) are always allowed and must NOT be listed here.

# Wrapper-lane test fixtures configure a synthetic git author so historical-ref
# scenarios can commit inside a throwaway fixture repo. `.local` is mDNS
# (RFC 6762), not on the scanner's reserved-TLD auto-allow list, so the fixture
# domain is vouched for here. It is not a personal address and never routes.
@sst3.local
